# country|broadcaster|rumbleEmbedId|expectedAuthor
#
# Pinned Rumble embed IDs. Re-check with: python scripts/check-rumble.py
#
# The embed ID is NOT the URL slug — rumble.com/v2o2oe5-... embeds as v2lh8yh,
# and using the slug returns 410. Resolve a new one with Rumble's oEmbed API:
#
#   curl "https://rumble.com/api/Media/oembed.json?url=<video page url>"
#
# expectedAuthor is the channel Rumble reports as owning the video. The checker
# drops any ID whose author stops matching, which is what keeps a third-party
# re-upload from inheriting a broadcaster's slot: searching Rumble for "RT news"
# returns v442j46, owned by an account called Kane2030, not by RT.
Russia|RT|vtp5hp|RT
Iran|Press TV|v4etgb3|Press TV
